6 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "60d65c05-8180-5d09-9673-b4401c622309" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050942 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050942 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186152112 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050942 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186152113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050942 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186152114 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050942 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186152115 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050942 #edb/ref 1031 "Further Percentages in Commerce and Finance" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050942 #edb/ref 1033 2563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050942 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "73c45326-98e6-548f-bbd4-a083816addc8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147148 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13066" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147148 #edb/ref 1071 "If $0$ then what is the missing number?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147148 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e650884c-e858-5213-8ff4-a39f9358edc0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147148 #edb/ref 1074 "We are given that the part is $36$, the percentage is $50\\%$, and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{whole} = \\textrm{part} \\div \\textrm{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $50\\%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{50}{100} = \\dfrac{50\\div 50}{100\\div 50} = \\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nwhole &= 36 \\div 50% \\\\\n&= 36 \\div \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n&= 36 \\cdot \\frac{2}{1} \\\\\n&= 36 \\cdot 2 \\\\\n&= 72\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147149 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13067" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147149 #edb/ref 1071 "$34\\%$ of a number is $170$. What is the number?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147149 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4bfda07b-18fd-541a-a627-ef7f1e47f41a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147149 #edb/ref 1074 "We're given that the part is $170$, the percentage is $34\\%$, and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{whole} = \\textrm{part} \\div \\textrm{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $34\\%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{34}{100} = \\dfrac{34\\div 2}{100\\div 2} = \\dfrac{17}{50}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nwhole &= 170 \\div 34% \\\\\n&= 170 \\div \\frac{17}{50} \\\\\n&= 170 \\cdot \\frac{50}{17} \\\\\n&= \\frac{170}{17} \\cdot 50 \\\\\n&= 10 \\cdot 50 \\\\\n&= 500\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147150 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13068" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147150 #edb/ref 1071 "In the math club, there are $16$ girls and some boys. If the girls represent $40\\%$ of the total members of the club, how many members does the math club have?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147150 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bd7aaf49-0da5-53c8-a5ee-863523548957" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147150 #edb/ref 1074 "We're given a part and a percentage, and we need to find the whole.\n\nIn this case, the part is the number of girls in the math club, which is $16$. The percentage is $40\\%$, and the whole is the total number of club members.\n\nTo find the whole, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{whole} = \\textrm{part} \\div \\textrm{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $40\\%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{40}{100} = \\dfrac{40\\div 20}{100\\div 20} = \\dfrac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nwhole &= 16 \\div 40% \\\\\n&= 16 \\div \\frac{2}{5} \\\\\n&= 16 \\cdot \\frac{5}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{16}{2} \\cdot 5 \\\\\n&= 8 \\cdot 5 \\\\\n&= 40\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the club has $40$ members." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147575 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147575 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147575 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147575 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147575 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding a Total Given a Part and a Multiple of Ten Percent" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147575 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186147148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147575 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "bb8b97e4-704c-5b13-97c7-6eb97aca392f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147576 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147847 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147576 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147879 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147576 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding a Total Given a Part and a Percentage" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147576 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186147149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147576 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "99c69dea-ec5d-525d-ae0f-da30e342fe63" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147577 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147845 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147577 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186147881 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147577 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding a Total Given a Part and a Percentage: Word Problems" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147577 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186147150 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147577 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "1670b7f6-fdee-5358-b145-9254e2a4ba50" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147657 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186148535 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147657 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186148536 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147657 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186148537 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147657 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186148538 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147657 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147657 #edb/ref 1045 "Finding a Total Given a Part and a Percentage" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147657 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186148535 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147657 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050386 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186147657 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "3903e573-e595-5f4d-8dbd-a1c1b28ab808" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148535 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148536 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148535 #edb/ref 1061 72289 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148535 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e956a0b5-6283-59e2-b00b-6fff43cb6aaf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148535 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186148781 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148536 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148537 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148536 #edb/ref 1061 72290 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148536 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "20f09f61-d500-5013-be0d-df259b534912" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148536 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147575 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148537 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186148538 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148537 #edb/ref 1061 72293 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148537 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "58253af5-26fc-5261-b61b-97788f445428" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148537 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148538 #edb/ref 1061 72296 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148538 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9f86a1a0-8db6-5c95-9948-5487d96d589a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148538 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186147577 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148781 #edb/ref 1064 "To find a part given a percent and whole, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{percent} \\times \\textrm{whole} = \\textrm{part}\n$$\n\nHowever, we sometimes want to find a whole given a part and a percent. To do this, we can use the relationship between multiplication and division to rewrite the above formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{whole} = \\textrm{part} \\div \\textrm{percent}\n$$\n\nLet's use this formula to find the missing number in the following statement:\n$0$\n\nIn this case, the part is $540$, and the percent is $30\\%$.\n\nWe can express $30\\%$ as a fraction as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{30}{100} = \\dfrac{30\\div 10}{100\\div 10} = \\dfrac{3}{10}\n$$\n\nPutting these numbers into our formula for the whole, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nwhole &= part \\div percent \\\\\n&= 540 \\div 30% \\\\\n&= 540 \\div \\frac{3}{10} \\\\\n&= 540 \\cdot \\frac{10}{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{540}{3} \\cdot 10 \\\\\n&= 180 \\cdot 10 \\\\\n&= 1, 800\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $1,800$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148781 #edb/ref 1065 8170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148781 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "69026176-778a-58ea-8ccf-185968679bd3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148781 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
